  "election_date": "2026-11-03",
  "description": "The 2026 Alaska gubernatorial election will be held on November 3, 2026, to elect the next governor and lieutenant governor of Alaska. Incumbent Republican Governor Mike Dunleavy is term-limited and ineligible to seek a third consecutive term, creating an open seat in a state where Republicans hold a triplex. A nonpartisan blanket primary will be held on August 18, 2026, with the top four candidates advancing to a ranked-choice general election. The race features a large and diverse field of 17 registered candidates, including 11 Republicans, 3 Democrats, and 3 independents/nonpartisans, reflecting both the competitiveness of the open seat and Alaska's unique top-four primary system.",
  "polling": [],
  "polling_note": "No specific general election matchup polls for this race were found as of June 2026. The primary is not until August 18, 2026, and most public polling has focused on hypothetical matchups involving candidates who chose to run for other offices. Polling is expected to increase after the top-four primary field is set.",
